  59: **Corollary 3.** Assume Theorems 1 and 2, the fivefold exclusion of §2 and the published fourfold exclusion
  60: (arXiv:2506.00224, §6.2). Then every set of at least 33 points in general position without a convex 7-gon has one of
  61: two forms:
  62: - it has no nontrivial symmetry; or
  63: - its symmetry group is exactly the half-turn group C2, and it then has an even number of points, at least 34.
  64: 
  65: Proof:
  66: - A finite symmetry group fixes the centroid, so it is cyclic or dihedral. Reflections are excluded by Theorem 2.
  67: - A rotation of order s >= 7 has orbits that are regular s-gons, so it gives a convex 7-gon.
  68: - Orders 3, 4 and 5 are excluded by deleting whole orbits. Order 6 contains order 3.
  69: - What remains is the half-turn. Its centre is collinear with every antipodal pair, so it is not a point of the set, and
  70:   the size is even.
  71: 
  72: The same holds for affine symmetries, after a change of inner product that makes the finite group orthogonal.
